title: Check block inherents with the runtime that built the block

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `sp_block_builder::check_inherents` and `check_inherents_with_data` now call the runtime's
    `check_inherents` API in the on-chain call context (`CallContext::Onchain { import: false }`),
    the context the block builder produces blocks in. With delayed runtime upgrades
    (`system_version >= 3`) the first block after the upgrade block is built by the new runtime,
    which is staged in `:pending_code`, while a runtime API call in the default off-chain context
    still runs the old one. The old runtime fails to decode any inherent whose encoding changed
    with the upgrade, so every node but the author rejected the block and the chain forked per
    authority. The AURA and BABE verifiers and the Cumulus import queues go through these helpers
    and are fixed by this change.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    In the on-chain context the new runtime checks the first post-upgrade block on top of the
    state the old runtime left behind, before the upgrade's migrations ran. The new
    `frame_executive::Executive::ensure_runtime_upgrade_applied` runs the pending
    `on_runtime_upgrade` hooks and records `LastRuntimeUpgrade` when the runtime version changed,
    and is a no-op otherwise. Call it first in your `BlockBuilder::check_inherents` implementation
    so that the inherent checks read storage in the layout the new runtime expects; the state
    changes of the API call are discarded. The runtimes in this repository are updated
    accordingly.

